 "capsule": "Communist Cuba denotes the one-party socialist state consolidated by Fidel Castro after the 1959 revolution, formally declared Marxist-Leninist in 1961 and organized under the Communist Party of Cuba from 1965, surviving the 1961 Bay of Pigs invasion, the 1962 missile crisis, decades of U.S. embargo, and the economic 'Special Period' after the 1991 Soviet collapse. Fidel Castro ceded power to his brother Raúl in 2006 (formalized 2008), with Miguel Díaz-Canel becoming the first non-Castro president in 2018 and first party secretary in 2021. This revolutionary socialist state is distinct from the pre-1959 'Republic of Cuba' sharing this Wikidata identifier.",
